  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 139 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nCurrent water vapor imagery and RAP analysis highlight broad ridging \nover the central CONUS as a shortwave tracks eastward over Montana. \nThis ridge is expected to linger over the forecast area through the \nbeginning of this week and allow for dry and hot conditions to\npersist across the region. As the prior discussion pointed out,\nthis upper feature will shift eastward by mid-week which may\nallow for slightly lower temperatures toward the latter half of\nthe week. However, this relief should be limited in nature as \nhigh pressure aloft builds in by next weekend. As a result, \ndaytime highs in the upper 90s and low 100s alongside lows in \nthe middle to upper 70s are forecast through the work week, and \nchances for meaningful rainfall over the next seven days appear \nunlikely at this time.",
